  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the sum of pairwise differences of outcomes. In this case, the pairwise differences are |4000 - 3000| = 1000 and |0 - 0| = 0, so the sum is 1000 for both lotteries (since the difference between 0 and 0 is zero). The sum is identical for both lotteries, so the reason would be indifferent. However, the individual does not mention this sum or any pairwise differences at all. Instead, they explicitly state that they evaluate expected value. Therefore, the information considered (expected values) does not match the information required by the decision reason (sum of pairwise outcome differences). Furthermore, the justification (choosing the lottery with higher expected value) does not align with the rule of the decision reason (which is based on sum of outcome differences). Since the individual neither considers nor justifies the sum of pairwise differences, the decision reason was not used. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

